{
  "summary": "This experiment tested multiprofile aggregation (avgpool) on the RNA-only PCA-2000 branch, changing only the profile setting from single to multi relative to llm_summary_001 while holding encoder, modality, and fusion fixed. The validation accuracy improved to ~0.591 (F1: ~0.573) from the single-profile baseline of ~0.485 (F1: ~0.464), indicating that multiprofile aggregation via avgpool yields a meaningful gain over the single-profile configuration under this encoder. It remains uncertain whether alternative aggregation strategies (e.g., maxpool, attention-weighted) could further improve performance, and whether this multiprofile advantage persists when the RNA branch is combined with image modality or fusion in downstream multimodal configurations."
}

